  },
  "Altruistic_Catalysts": {
    "is_used": "No",
    "explanation": "While leaders are acting for the public good, the text does not portray them as challenging a status quo through rebellion, enduring extreme personal hardship/sacrifice (Martyr), or fighting against oppression in the sense of an Underdog narrative. They are depicted as established authorities maintaining order rather than catalysts for systemic liberation or radical change."
